---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Prose from '../components/Prose.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';

// FINAL: legal text v5, adopted 13–0 on 2026-11-17 (file SHA-256 fc0e5514…f052). Word for word; change it only with
// Christian's approval.
const email = site.contactEmail;
const mail = `mailto:${email}`;
---

<Layout title="disclaimer" description="Cueory is a study aid, not medical advice." noindex>
  <Prose>
    <h1>disclaimer</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-ink-soft">Last updated 17 November 2026</p>

    <p>
      Cueory is for nursing students to practice and review what they’re learning. It does not provide medical, nursing or
      clinical advice or replace instruction or supervised clinical training. Never use Cueory to make a decision about a
      real patient, check a medication dose for care, or decide what to do about your own or someone else’s health.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>In an emergency, call 911 in the United States or your local emergency number.</strong> In a clinical
      facility, alert staff immediately and follow the facility’s emergency procedures. Cueory is not monitored for
      emergencies and cannot respond to one.
    </p>

    <h2>Protect patient information</h2>
    <p>
      Use invented examples only. Keep information about real patients off Cueory and out of emails to us, even if you
      leave out their names. Photos, screenshots, dates, room numbers and details from a clinical placement can identify
      someone.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you send us patient information by mistake, promptly follow your school’s or facility’s reporting procedure.
      Start a new email to <a href={mail}>{email}</a> with the approximate time and where you sent it so we can locate it
      and address the disclosure. Do not forward the original, attach a screenshot or repeat any patient details.
    </p>

    <h2>Follow your school’s and clinical site’s rules</h2>
    <p>
      Use Cueory during an exam or graded assignment only if the rules for that activity expressly allow it. Keep
      confidential questions and answers to yourself, including anything recalled from an exam. In clinical placements
      and at work, follow facility policies and ask your instructor, preceptor or supervising clinician about patient
      care.
    </p>

    <h2>Check what you learn</h2>
    <p>
      Some study activities are samples, and some pages contain placeholder text. Material may lack citations or review
      by a licensed nurse. Check what you learn against your assigned materials and current textbooks. If sources
      disagree, ask your instructor before relying on the information. To flag a possible error, email the page title or
      link and a description to <a href={mail}>{email}</a>. Leave out patient details and confidential exam material.
    </p>
    <p>
      The daily puzzles currently use everyday words. Some repeat. Neither a puzzle result nor a practice score tells you
      whether you’re ready to care for patients or pass an exam. Using Cueory does not guarantee a grade, a passing score
      on the NCLEX or any other exam outcome.
    </p>
    <p>
      Cueory is independent. No school, nursing program, testing organization or licensing board runs or endorses it.
      Names and marks belonging to those organizations remain theirs.
    </p>

    <p><a href="/terms">Terms of Use</a> · <a href="/privacy">Privacy Notice</a></p>
  </Prose>
</Layout>
